### My intuition in one sentence

**Based on what I currently know, I would not be upset that she wasn't automatically prescribed an antiviral. I would call it a borderline case where a careful doctor would assess her COVID risk factors, and if she is otherwise a healthy vaccinated 33-year-old, probably choose supportive care.**

What I *would* care about more today is whether the fever finally starts trending down, whether her oxygen/breathing remain normal, and whether the 5-day high-fever illness develops any signs suggesting a complication.

If you tell me her **vaccination status, approximate BMI/weight, whether she smokes, and whether she has any other chronic diseases**, I can move this from “borderline” to a much more confident yes/no assessment.

